-- title:
--   Points of the Kummer cover $y^n=f(x)$: evaluation homomorphisms and the local coordinate $x-a$
-- statement:
--   Let $n\in\mathbb N$, $f\in\mathbb C[x]$, and let $R_{n,f}=\mathbb C[x][Y]/(Y^n-f)$ be the coordinate ring of the Kummer cover $y^n=f(x)$, with $y$ the class of $Y$.
--
--   The file defines two objects. For a point $(a,b)\in\mathbb C^2$ of the curve, that is with $b^n=f(a)$, the evaluation homomorphism
--   $$\mathrm{ev}_{a,b}:R_{n,f}\longrightarrow\mathbb C,\qquad x\longmapsto a,\qquad y\longmapsto b,$$
--   whose kernel is a prime ideal; and, for $a\in\mathbb C$, the element $x-a\in R_{n,f}$.
--
--   The rest of the file establishes, with proofs, the local structure that later parts use:
--
--   1. for $n\ge1$, $R_{n,f}$ is integral over $\mathbb C[x]$, and its maximal ideals are exactly the kernels $\ker\mathrm{ev}_{a,b}$ with $b^n=f(a)$;
--   2. for $n\ge1$, in a localization of $R_{n,f}$ at $\ker\mathrm{ev}_{a,b}$ the maximal ideal is generated by $x-a$ when $f(a)\ne0$, and by $y$ when $f(a)=0$ and $f$ is squarefree;
--   3. for $n\ge1$ and $f$ squarefree of positive degree, $Y^n-f$ is irreducible over $\mathbb C(x)$, $R_{n,f}$ is a Noetherian domain, its localizations at the points $(a,b)$ are discrete valuation rings, and $R_{n,f}$ is a Dedekind domain.
--
--   These identify the finite places of the Kummer field $\mathbb C(x)[Y]/(Y^n-f)$ and their uniformizers, as needed to compute the genus three of $\operatorname{Re}(z^4)=1$, that is, of $y^4=2-x^4$, in Remark 5.
--
--   **Formalization Note**: A point is passed together with a proof of $b^n=f(a)$; the condition $n\ne0$ is the instance `NeZero n`, and the conditions that $f$ is squarefree and has positive degree are `Fact` instances. The statements about local rings hold for any ring presented as the localization at $\ker\mathrm{ev}_{a,b}$.
-- source:
--   C. Perassi, Sharp symmetry bounds for real algebraic curves (note), definitions of the formalization, https://github.com/carlok/curve-symmetry-lean/blob/d99bc17a1c397956c05d7417de50f9beed56580f/sharp_symmetry_bounds.pdf. Lean modules KummerLocal in https://github.com/carlok/curve-symmetry-lean/tree/d99bc17a1c397956c05d7417de50f9beed56580f/lean (C. Perassi)

